{"type":"npc","name":"Gasbelly Goblin","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":42,"temp":0,"max":42,"details":""},"ac":{"value":18,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":20}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"piercing","value":5,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"slashing","value":3,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","goblin"],"details":""},"level":{"value":3},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>The drive to find new ways to start fires leads some goblins to dabble in alchemy. All too often, their penchant for ingesting untested concoctions dooms these amateur alchemists to a quick, explosive end. Those who survive their experiments occasionally gain unexpected abilities. And these successful innovators tend to inspire others to follow in their footsteps.</p><p>One of these successful mutations produces gasbelly goblins. While goblins are already recognized for their iron stomachs, gasbelly goblins take this ability to new heights. They can fill their stomachs with hazardous concoctions that mix into poisonous gases. These gases swell their stomachs to gruesome sizes, making the thrilled goblins lighter than the air. While airborne, they can propel themselves through the air by belching with great force, trailing a noxious green cloud in their wake.</p><p>Gasbellies regularly test their digestive systems in elaborate eating contests, which usually end in a chorus of vile belches. Their immunity to poison makes them reckless, so contests often end with stomachaches and broken teeth. Gasbelly goblins also almost universally develop a love of eggs. Several gasbelly tribes have turned satisfying their eggy cravings into a perilous sport, conducting daring aerial raids on high eyries in search of the eggs of large animals like griffons and hippogriffs. Less ethically minded gasbellies do not limit their diets to animals, stealing eggs from intelligent creatures like manticores or even drakes if they believe they can get away with it. Inevitably, such attempts inspire rage in their targets, who are rarely satisfied to limit their vengeance to the offending goblins.</p><h2>Gasbelly Heroes</h2><p>Gasbelly goblins speak in reverent tones about those among them who consume rocks, metal, or even more exotic substances such as electricity, flames, or void energy. Whether these gasbelly heroes truly exist or are simply the products of the goblins' wishful thinking remains a matter of debate.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 7/18/30 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light, medium), shield, skill items (Acrobatics, Crafting)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), intelligence, poison, poisonous armor, sensory (darkvision), sturdy, throwing, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Rodney Sloan","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":1},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":0},"cha":{"mod":1}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":8,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":5,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":10,"special":[{"label":"to Maneuver in Flight","predicate":["action:maneuver-in-flight"],"base":6}]},"crafting":{"base":10,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["goblin","humanoid"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"i5YkN1V3TZw9VGWz","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/a